  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Performing by the Book? is already showing a modest but meaningful footprint: it has 1,404 OAPEN downloads, has been discussed in two Orpheus Instituut YouTube sessions, and appears in a small amount of public discourse captured by Crossref. The record is still early in citation terms, with OpenAlex currently showing no citations, but the book is clearly being read and introduced to audiences beyond the page.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Published by Leuven University Press in 2024 as part of the Orpheus Institute Series, Performing by the Book? has gained attention through readership and structured scholarly engagement rather than citation accumulation. The strongest signal is use: OAPEN records 1,404 downloads, indicating substantial access to the open version. That pattern suggests the book is being actively consulted, likely by readers working across music, interpretation, aesthetics, and related humanities fields reflected in its conceptual profile.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The book is also present in teaching and learning contexts. Two Orpheus Instituut YouTube sessions explicitly discuss it, which points to uptake in a mediated educational or research-seminar setting. Such appearances do not amount to scholarly citation, but they do show the book being used to frame discussion and introduce its arguments to a wider specialist audience.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Public discourse signals are limited but nonzero: Crossref-based attention records two mentions, indicating that the title has entered some circulating scholarly conversation. At the same time, the citation record in OpenAlex remains at zero, so the work’s longer-term scholarly uptake has not yet emerged in citation-based indicators. This is not unusual for a recent book, especially one whose dissemination may still be unfolding.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the record points to a book with clear early visibility, strong open access readership, and some evidence of pedagogical and public-facing discussion. The pattern is consistent with a title that is being read and introduced within its specialist community, even while formal citation impact is still in its early stages.</p>",
